Feature: An automated approval verdict is durable on HEAD, not only on disk

  # BL-892 approval-flip-commits-01
  Scenario: Approve leaves human_approval: approved on HEAD
    Given a live ticket whose human_approval is pending
    When an automated Approve action records the verdict successfully
    Then git show HEAD for that ticket file contains "human_approval: approved"
    And the action reports success only after that commit lands

  # BL-892 approval-flip-commits-02
  Scenario: Reject and Amend are equally durable
    Given a live ticket whose human_approval is pending
    When an automated Reject action records a reason successfully
    Then git show HEAD for that ticket file contains "human_approval: rejected"
    When a different live pending ticket receives an automated Amend with a note
    Then git show HEAD for that ticket file contains "human_approval: amending"

  # BL-892 approval-flip-commits-03
  Scenario: Commit failure is never reported as an unqualified success
    Given a live ticket whose human_approval is pending
    And the commit-integrity helper will fail for this write
    When an automated Approve action runs
    Then the action does not report unqualified success
    And the durability failure is observable to the human

  # BL-892 approval-flip-commits-04
  Scenario: Expedite still commits through the same integrity helper
    Given a live paused ticket whose human_approval is pending
    When an automated Expedite action records approval and promotion successfully
    Then git show HEAD for that ticket file contains "human_approval: approved"
    And the commit went through commit_integrity_cli (pathspec-scoped)
